  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">BIOFIN agreement 2023-2026</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Biodiversity Finance Initiative (BIOFIN) Phase II (2018 &#x2013; 2027) acts as a global knowledge network and supports countries to implement National Biodiversity Finance Plans and finance solutions to achieve tangible finance results. The BIOFIN program include actions to (1) help reduce or redirect resources causing harm to biodiversity, (2) generate additional resources or (3) enhance the effectiveness of resource use, and (4) prevent future costs. BIOFIN is tailored to accelerate the implementation of the CBD Global Biodiversity Framework, contributing to multiple targets.

Countries supported in this agreement: Bhutan, Brazil, Cambodia, China, Colombia, Costa Rica, Ethiopia, Gabon, Indonesia, India, Kenya, Madagascar, Malawi, Nepal, Peru, Tanzania, Uganda, Vietnam

Global activites aslo include:
- Guidance for achieving GBF Target 15
- A new e-learning module on biodiversity finance solutions
- Gender mainstreaming: BIOFIN will scale up its focus on promoting gender equality and include more guidance on integrating gender into biodiversity finance solutions. This will be reported on.

Many of the financial solutions also have a positive impact for climate adaptation and mitigation and there is an increased  focus on integrating climate in general in the biodiversity finance plans. BIFOFIN will report on climate through one mitigation-indicator and one adaptation-indicators.</narrative>
  </description>
